&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently we&amp;rsquo;ve been working on a identity for a hydrologist. We picked &amp;ldquo;Purista&amp;rdquo; as a leading typeface. It was ment mostly for stationery and hydrologic reports – both headlines and body text and we&amp;rsquo;re happy with it&amp;rsquo;s tech look. Unfortunately, we encountered a serious issue with mathematical symbos and greek, wich Purista does not support.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Logo, Font &amp; Lettering Bible</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/42010/</link><pubDate>Tue, 12 Feb 2008 10:52:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/42010/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/"&gt;Logo, Font &amp;amp; Lettering.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>